WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.960
Circular knitting on the Titexma TH/TR 160

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.080
has one more step than
some other machines.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.840
The secret to circular or tubular knitting

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:16.600
on any machine is to understand
the slip settings on each bed.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.680
The difference with this machine is

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.920
that it only has one slip
setting on the main bed.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.880
With the carriage set in this position,

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:31.320
the carriage will slip in both directions.
On the ribber,

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.160
you can choose to slip
in only one direction.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.680
Get started in circular knitting on this

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.560
machine with both beds
set for plain knitting.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:49.680
Cast on and knit full needle rib
with all needles in work on both beds.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.200
Make sure the ribber is racked to "H" so

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.680
the needles aren't crashing
into each other, and knit a few rows.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:02.760
End with your carriage on the right.
For the first row of circular knitting.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:07.840
Leave the main bed carriage set for plain.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:16.320
The change lever will be set to plane
and the side cam levers are set on "N".

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.240
On the ribber,
set it to slip left by putting the left

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:28.720
side cam lever to print and make
sure the tuck lever is set on "R".

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:34.520
In this example, the ribber will slip
as you pass the carriage to the left.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:40.160
So knit across and only
the main bed stitches will knit.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:44.560
Now, keeping those ribber settings
the same throughout the whole piece,

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:50.880
move the main bed change lever to "part",
knit to the right.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.560
Only the ribber needles will knit.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.600
You'll repeat rows 1 and 2

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:01.720
for circular knitting
and you'll change the main bed setting

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:06.560
every other row, keeping the ribber
setting the same throughout.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.320
Row 1, your main bed
carriage is set to plain.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:15.400
You knit to the left and you'll
knit the main bed only.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:18.200
Row 2, the main bed carriage is set

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:25.280
to part and you'll knit to the right,
and ribber stitches will knit only.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.760
So you'll change that main bed setting

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:34.680
every other row from part to plane,
part to plain every other row.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:43.160
With circular knitting,
you're alternating knitting on the ribber

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:46.320
and knitting on the main bed,
forming a tube.

